<title>FRANCE: Total sees no refining problems till weekend.</title>
<headline>Total sees no refining problems till weekend.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>French oil group Total SA said it had no problems keeping its French refineries running at capacity at least until the weekend, despite strike action by truckers.</p>
<p>&quot;We do not have the problems in La Mede (near Marseilles) of other refineries and we do not expect problems until at least the weekend. That is not to say that there are no blockades by truckers and products cannot leave normally but production is continuing,&quot; a company spokeswoman said.</p>
</text>
